12. Kubernetes Workflow (End-to-End)
From Code to Running Application

Developer: Write code and commit (git push).

CI Pipeline: Build, test, and run checks (Jenkins, GitLab CI).

Build Image: Build Docker image and push to registry (docker build & push).

Container Registry: Store image in registry (Docker Hub, ECR, ACR).

Deploy: Apply manifests (kubectl apply -f).

Kubernetes Cluster: Scheduler places Pods on available Nodes (kubectl get pods).

Service Exposure: Expose via Service/Ingress (ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer).

Monitor & Scale: Monitor logs, metrics, and auto-scale (Prometheus, Grafana).

📋 Common Resources in Flow
Deployment / StatefulSet: Manage stateless or stateful applications.

Pod: Smallest deployable unit.

Service: Stable networking to access Pods.

ConfigMap / Secret: Non-sensitive and sensitive data.

PersistentVolumeClaim: Claim storage.

Ingress: HTTP/HTTPS routing.

NetworkPolicy: Control traffic.

ServiceAccount & RBAC: Identity and access control.
